  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Fig. 8, 'Linkage across classifications, generic products and trade items'. Three columns: CLASSIFICATION (classes or groups of diseases, pathogens or drugs); PRODUCT (name/INN, strength, dosage form, route of administration); and TRADE ITEM (unique identifier such as a GTIN, brand name, manufacturer, country of origin, packaging details, volumetrics, shelf life). The example row traces Nervous system → Analgesics → Other analgesics and antipyretics → Anilides → Paracetamol to the product 'Paracetamol 500 mg tablet'. That product branches into two manufacturers' trade items, each with its own unique IDs and pack hierarchy: a case and inner pack of 100 from ABC Manufacturing (brand Ceta123), and a case, inner pack of 50 and each of 10 from XYZ Manufacturing (brand ParaXYZ). A bottom row gives each column's use: strategic (data aggregation and analysis), tactical (forecasting, procurement planning and aggregate visibility) and operational (inventory, distribution, tracking and tracing, pharmacovigilance and AEFI analysis).",
